+### The push–pullback cycle
+
+Once a person has completed one fat-loss phase and reversed out properly, ongoing physique management is described as alternating between lean gaining and short pullbacks rather than repeated full cuts:
+
+- Lean gain at roughly **1 lb per week**.
+- Every **8–16 weeks**, run a **four-week mini cut** pulling back **4–5 lb**.
+- Resume gaining.
+
+Each cycle is characterized as "a bit more muscle, a bit less fat," repeated year over year, with maintenance calories climbing over time — the stated personal endpoint being maintenance at around 3,000 calories, contrasted against the impossibility of holding the same physique at 1,800.
+
